TIP:  If transposing, play the root chord of the (CaddG) and (Gadd) and add the 5th note as needed.

TIP:  The (CaddG) can be omitted in the third line alternating (CaddG) and (C) sequence but just involves adding and removing the pinky to the 1st string/3rd fret to accentuate the upward inflection at the point where Reba sings it. 

TIP:  An (F8) ends the song.  It's high <c> on the piano and played up as a (C) on the 8th fret with your pinky covering the bass <c>.  Or just play (C).
    
      
